// Day 20: Scheduled task creation on the lab endpoint
//
// What it looks for: ScheduledTaskCreated events. They live in DeviceEvents, not
// DeviceRegistryEvents (my first attempt queried the wrong table and returned zero rows).
// ATT&CK T1053.005.
//
// How to read it: the task details are packed into AdditionalFields as JSON (task name,
// trigger, action, subject user). The initiating-process columns are empty on this event
// type, so the schtasks.exe command line comes from the alert story instead.
// InitiatingProcessLogonId can be matched against the alert's "Subject logon id".
//
// Result in my lab (Atomic Red Team T1053.005 test 2): one row at 4:06:41 PM.
//   TaskName \spawn, a time trigger at 2026-10-05T20:10:00, action C:\windows\system32\cmd.exe,
//   subject user UserA.
DeviceEvents
| where DeviceName =~ "mdf-dt-w11"
| where ActionType == "ScheduledTaskCreated"
| project Timestamp, DeviceName, ActionType, AdditionalFields, InitiatingProcessAccountName, InitiatingProcessLogonId
